From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: amortize native Direct Switch TX polls

Native Direct Switch returns permanently mapped buffers to its pool, so
normal TX completions need neither skb delivery nor DMA unmapping. Follow
QSDK's PPE TX completion accounting: reap up to four completions per NAPI
budget unit, retaining a bounded batch and charging its rounded-up cost
to the shared NAPI. This amortizes ring locks, tail-pointer publication,
RX refill retries and cross-engine index synchronization across a batch.

Do not publish a WLAN completion tail pointer when the poll did not reap
any entries. Preserve exception handling, all descriptor validation and
the existing PPDU and monitor statistics configuration.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ppe_ds.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ppe_ds.c
@@ -554,9 +554,15 @@ int ath12k_wifi7_ds_service(struct ath12k_dp *dp, int budget)
 	u32 cookie, info;
 	unsigned int completed = 0, acked = 0, dropped = 0;
 	int done = 0;
+	int quota;
 
-	if (!ds || !ds->complete_ready || READ_ONCE(ds->stopped))
+	if (!ds || !ds->complete_ready || READ_ONCE(ds->stopped) || budget <= 0)
 		return 0;
+	/* QSDK charges four lightweight PPE completions per NAPI budget unit.
+	 * Bound each batch and round its cost up so a full batch requests
+	 * another poll instead of completing NAPI with work on the ring.
+	 */
+	quota = (budget << 2) - 1;
 	__skb_queue_head_init(&reinject);
 	srng = ath12k_ds_srng(ds, &ds->complete);
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&srng->lock, flags);
@@ -566,7 +572,7 @@ int ath12k_wifi7_ds_service(struct ath12k_dp *dp, int budget)
 	 * packet separately; publish the counters once after the batch.
 	 */
 	spin_lock(&ds->tx_lock);
-	while (done < budget) {
+	while (done < quota) {
 		status = ath12k_hal_srng_dst_get_next_entry(dp->ab, srng);
 		if (!status)
 			break;
@@ -625,7 +631,8 @@ int ath12k_wifi7_ds_service(struct ath12k_dp *dp, int budget)
 		WRITE_ONCE(ds->faulted, true);
 	}
 	spin_unlock(&ds->tx_lock);
-	ath12k_hal_srng_access_end(dp->ab, srng);
+	if (done)
+		ath12k_hal_srng_access_end(dp->ab, srng);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&srng->lock, flags);
 	atomic64_add(completed, &ds->tx_completed);
 	atomic64_add(acked, &ds->tx_acked);
@@ -640,7 +647,7 @@ int ath12k_wifi7_ds_service(struct ath12k_dp *dp, int budget)
 		qcom_ppe_ds_sync(ds->handle);
 	if (READ_ONCE(ds->faulted))
 		ath12k_ds_fault(ds);
-	return done;
+	return (done + 3) >> 2;
 }
 
 /* control_lock held. The hardware rings stay registered across a VAP's
